    rdfs:comment "1.11.0 (2026-11-14): Chapter 19 deck 2.2.0: story slides told as natural prose with no WHO/WHAT labels (the owner's standing storytelling rule, missed in 2.0.0 and 2.1.0); new story prose check."@en .

ex:TK8_BuildDeck_Ch19 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:hasAuditNote "Deck 2.2.0 (03-materials/ch19/SEN0414_Ch19_TimeScheduling_3e_v2_2_0.pptx, 42 slides, 18 examples) replaces 2.1.0 and 2.0.0; 2.2.0 tells every story as three natural prose paragraphs with no WHO/WHAT/WHEN labels (my miss: earlier versions carried the labelled layout over from chapter 18; the new 08-tooling/sen0414_story_prose_check_v1_0_0.py fails the old deck with 42 findings and passes 2.2.0) after the owner's rulings of 2026-11-14 (handover v1.1.0). All 8 automatic conditions of 08-tooling/cme_material_check_v1_0_0.py pass (titles of 4 or more words, a visual on every content slide, notes of 60 to 140 words, no prompt markers, every code frame parses, no lambda); the two named conditions (page runs the Slide code tab, taught-only) are not built in the tool and are not claimed. Reviewed conditions (academician, faculty reviewer, undergraduate reader) are NOT yet recorded. Builder's own manifest check 2.1.0 PASS; overlap check CLEAN; links unchanged. The old standard check v1.0.0 finds code boxes by the '>>> ' prompt and v1.1.0 caps notes at 60 words, so both conflict with the rulings and are not used as the release gate; their v1.1.0 output is kept in logs_v2_1_0 for the record. Deviations from the approved draft stay as recorded in v1.9.0." .
ex:ST8_BuildCh19 backlog:hasState backlog:InProgress ; backlog:hasAuditNote "Deck done under the rulings; page with the Slide code tab remains." .
